636 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 168 0 R/Pg 54 0 R/A[940 0 R 0]/K[9]>>
endobj

637 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 169 0 R/T(BACKGROUND. Preschool children spend a lot of time at home when their lungs are developing. Acute respiratory infections \(ARIs\) are the main cause of hospitalisations in preschool children and are associated with cold, damp housing. Preschool ARIs have lifelong health consequences.)/E(BACKGROUND. Preschool children spend a lot of time at home when their lungs are developing. Acute respiratory infections \(ARIs\) are the main cause of hospitalisations in preschool children and are associated with cold, damp housing. Preschool ARIs have lifelong health consequences.)/Pg 55 0 R/K[0]>>
endobj

638 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 169 0 R/T(Half of Scotland\220s housing has low energy efficiency. The Scottish Government is retrofitting housing to increase home energy efficiency \(HEE\) for Net Zero targets. However, whilst making homes warmer, some HEE measures reduce ventilation, decreasing heat loss but trapping air pollutants indoors, potentially worsening respiratory health.)/E(Half of Scotland\220s housing has low energy efficiency. The Scottish Government is retrofitting housing to increase home energy efficiency \(HEE\) for Net Zero targets. However, whilst making homes warmer, some HEE measures reduce ventilation, decreasing heat loss but trapping air pollutants indoors, potentially worsening respiratory health.)/Pg 55 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

639 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 169 0 R/T(We can now link children\220s healthcare data with every home they have lived in across Scotland. This new national linkage will allow us to investigate how underheated homes and the different approaches to warming them affect preschool ARI risk.)/E(We can now link children\220s healthcare data with every home they have lived in across Scotland. This new national linkage will allow us to investigate how underheated homes and the different approaches to warming them affect preschool ARI risk.)/Pg 55 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

640 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 169 0 R/T(OBJECTIVES. 1. Identify children living in underheated homes using routinely collected data. 2. Estimate how many preschool ARIs are due to underheated, damp homes. 3. Explore whether different ways of making homes warmer increase or decrease preschool ARI risk.)/E(OBJECTIVES. 1. Identify children living in underheated homes using routinely collected data. 2. Estimate how many preschool ARIs are due to underheated, damp homes. 3. Explore whether different ways of making homes warmer increase or decrease preschool ARI risk.)/Pg 55 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

641 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 169 0 R/T(PLANNED METHODS. We have established a retrospective birth cohort of children born in Scotland from 2008-2025 followed up until 5 years old. The cohort links cross-sectoral data from healthcare, housing, HEE measures, smart meters, air pollution, high street banking and weather for 4 million child-years and 230,000 properties across Scotland.)/E(PLANNED METHODS. We have established a retrospective birth cohort of children born in Scotland from 2008-2025 followed up until 5 years old. The cohort links cross-sectoral data from healthcare, housing, HEE measures, smart meters, air pollution, high street banking and weather for 4 million child-years and 230,000 properties across Scotland.)/Pg 55 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

642 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 169 0 R/T(Risk prediction models will identify underheated homes using routine data and we will estimate the contribution of underheated homes to preschool ARIs using causal epidemiology methods. We will use machine learning approaches and natural experiment methodology to determine the effects of different HEE measures on preschool ARI risk.)/E(Risk prediction models will identify underheated homes using routine data and we will estimate the contribution of underheated homes to preschool ARIs using causal epidemiology methods. We will use machine learning approaches and natural experiment methodology to determine the effects of different HEE measures on preschool ARI risk.)/Pg 55 0 R/K[5 6]>>
endobj

643 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 169 0 R/T(IMPACT. Results will inform energy, welfare, climate and building policies and ensure that Net Zero policies do not worsen health inequalities. The new methodology developed will be applicable to other health conditions, demographics and populations.)/E(IMPACT. Results will inform energy, welfare, climate and building policies and ensure that Net Zero policies do not worsen health inequalities. The new methodology developed will be applicable to other health conditions, demographics and populations.)/Pg 55 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

